Tools that we need to start.

1. Chocolatey — Super helpful for installing software easily on Windows. No more manual downloads

2. GitHub — Essential for version control. 

3.  AWS — Set up your cloud infrastructure. (You’ll need a card to register, but AWS Free Tier services are perfect for beginners)

4.  VSCode, Sublime Text, or Notepad++ — Use any IDE/editor you're comfortable with to start writing and managing code.

5. Oracle VM VirtualBox + Vagrant — Best combo to practice Infrastructure as Code (IaC) locally.

6.  Ansible — One of the simplest and most powerful tools for Configuration Management and Automation.

7. Docker and Kubernetes — Learn containerization and orchestration from scratch. 

8. Jenkins — Start building your first CI/CD pipelines. It’s open-source and extremely powerful once you get familiar.

9. Terraform — A widely used IaC tool for real-world infrastructure automation.

These are just the starting points. We use many other tools too, depending on the architecture, team needs, security requirements, monitoring needs, and more.
